-- title:
--   Residues of tube-bounded chart functions form a subalgebra
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $A$ a valuation subring of $L$ with residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, let $F$ be a field which is an $L$-algebra, and let $\bar F$ be a field which is a $\kappa$-algebra. Let $C$ be a `ComponentChart` for these data: a valuation subring $C.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism $C.\mathrm{residue} : C.\mathrm{integers} \to \bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a set $C.\mathrm{dom}$ of places of $F$ over $L$, a finite set $C.\mathrm{nodes}$ of places of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$, a map $C.\mathrm{placeMap}$ from places of $F/L$ to places of $\bar F/\kappa$, and the compatibility axioms of that structure (among them: $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,L\,F\,x \in C.\mathrm{integers}$ iff $x \in A$; the residue of a constant from $A$ is its image in $\kappa$; the pointwise law expressing, at a rational place $P \in C.\mathrm{dom}$ and for $f \in C.\mathrm{integers}$ lying in every valuation ring of places of $C.\mathrm{dom}$ with the same image under $C.\mathrm{placeMap}$, that $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$ and that its residue agrees with the residue of $C.\mathrm{residue}\,f$ at $C.\mathrm{placeMap}\,P$). Assume every $P \in C.\mathrm{dom}$ is rational, i.e. $\kappa$-- more precisely $L$ -- surjects onto the residue field of $P$. Let $g : \iota \to F$ be any family with $g\,i \in C.\mathrm{integers}$ and each $g\,i$ tube-bounded, meaning that for every $P \in C.\mathrm{dom}$ one has $g\,i \in P.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(g\,i) \in A$. Then for every $y$ in the $\kappa$-subalgebra of $\bar F$ generated by the residues $C.\mathrm{residue}\,(g\,i)$ there exist $f \in C.\mathrm{integers}$, tube-bounded, with $C.\mathrm{residue}\,f = y$.
--
--   This is the lifting step for component charts of a semistable model: residues of tube-bounded functions integral for the chart's Gauss valuation are closed under the $\kappa$-algebra operations, so any polynomial relation among residues can be realised upstairs. It is used in the construction of supersingular charts with local affinoid and node annuli on modular curves of full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_ComponentChart_exists_tubeBounded_residue_eq_of_mem_adjoin.lean

